      "side": 1,
      "message": "control_request 51 :\nSend a 51 control request (\"Get Protocol\") to figure out if the device supports the Android accessory protocol. A non-zero number is returned if the protocol is supported, which represents the version of the protocol that the device supports (currently, only version 1 exists). \n\ncontrol_request 52 :\nIf the device returns a proper protocol version, send identifying string information to the device. This information allows the device to figure out an appropriate application for this accessory and also present the user with a URL if an appropriate application does not exist. \n\nThe detail description could reference below link.\nhttps://tool.oschina.net/uploads/apidocs/android/tools/adk/aoa.html\n\nBelow document is show the uevent work.\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1hAmw41yn9ErT2O0DsMc7NPesF_BW3M0-g-OhjBhgznQ/edit",
